# Runtime settings for the edge container only. The edge mode itself
# (ATLAS_EDGE_MODE) lives in env/compose.env, because it also decides which
# ports are published and the portal needs the same value.
#
# Host names. Leave them EMPTY on a new installation: the first-run wizard
# stores the domains and the edge picks them up from installation.json within
# 5 seconds, without a restart. When set, these values WIN over the wizard.
# ATLAS_TRACKING_HOST may list several names separated by commas.
ATLAS_PORTAL_HOST=
ATLAS_TRACKING_HOST=
# Optional separate host for conversion postbacks. Without it postbacks are
# accepted on the tracking host.
ATLAS_POSTBACK_HOST=
# `proxy` mode only: the network of the TLS proxy or load balancer in front of
# Atlas. Only requests coming from it may report the client address and the
# original scheme; everything else is replaced with what the edge observed.
# Never widen it to a whole private range you do not control -- a wrong value
# makes every visitor look like one address, and lets a client forge its own.
# In `direct` mode there is no proxy and this value is ignored.
ATLAS_EDGE_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDR=127.0.0.1/32
